# 5-bit error correction encoding circuit
# Reference [12]: Knill et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 86, 5811 (2001), Fig. 1
# 5 qubits (q0=data=C1[12], q1=M, q2=C2[12], q3=C3[12], q4=C4[12]), 18 gates total
#
# NMR gate types: 1=single-qubit (Ry/Rx/Rz), 2=two-qubit (ZZ)
# T=1 for Ry(90)/Rx(90)/ZZ(90);  T=0 for Rz (free gate, rotating frame)
#
# Single-qubit gates from [12] Fig. 1 encoding network (top panel):
#   q1 (M):    Y90, Rz(free), X90   -- total T=2
#   q0 (data): X90                  -- total T=1
#   q2 (C2):   Y90, Y90             -- total T=2
#   q3 (C3):   X90, Y90             -- total T=2
#   q4 (C4):   X90                  -- total T=1
#
# ZZ interaction graph: path  q1 - q0 - q2 - q3 - q4
#   maps to trans-crotonic molecular chain: M(6)-C4(3)-C3(2)-C2(1)-C1(0)
#   where [12]'s C1=our C4(3), [12]'s C4=our C1(0)
#   fast W values along path: 20, 60, 36, 35
#
# NOTE: the [[5,1,3]] stabilizers (XZZXI,IXZZX,XIXZZ,ZXIXZ) in principle
# also require some non-adjacent interactions which force slow W values and
# drive the paper's 0.0779 s result.  Those pairs are not machine-readable
# from [12] Fig. 1, so this file reconstructs the chain backbone only.
5
# Phase 1: initialize ancilla qubits (level 0, simultaneous)
1 1 1.0 0    # Y90  on q1 (M)
1 2 1.0 0    # Y90  on q2 (C2[12])
1 3 1.0 0    # X90  on q3 (C3[12]), Rx(90)
# Phase 2: first ZZ + X90 on C4 (level 1)
2 1 0 1.0 1  # ZZ(q1,q0) = ZZ(M, C1[12])
1 4 1.0 1    # X90  on q4 (C4[12]), Rx(90)
# Phase 3: data qubit correction (level 2)
1 0 1.0 2    # X90  on q0 (data=C1[12]), Rx(90)
# Phase 4: second ZZ (level 3)
2 0 2 1.0 3  # ZZ(q0,q2) = ZZ(C1[12], C2[12])
# Phase 5: M frame correction + second Y90 on C2 (level 4)
1 1 0.0 4    # Rz   on q1 (Z270 frame correction, free)
1 2 1.0 4    # Y90  on q2 (C2[12]), second rotation
# Phase 6: third ZZ (level 5)
2 2 3 1.0 5  # ZZ(q2,q3) = ZZ(C2[12], C3[12])
# Phase 7: X90 on M + Y90 on C3 (level 6)
1 1 1.0 6    # X90  on q1 (M), second rotation, Rx(90)
1 3 1.0 6    # Y90  on q3 (C3[12]), second rotation
# Phase 8: fourth ZZ (level 7)
2 3 4 1.0 7  # ZZ(q3,q4) = ZZ(C3[12], C4[12])
# Phase 9: free Rz frame corrections (level 8)
1 0 0.0 8
1 1 0.0 8
1 2 0.0 8
1 3 0.0 8
1 4 0.0 8
